Multiple data recession Taiwan's economy performs poorly in the beginning of the year
Xinhua Taipei, February 11 (Xinhua reporters Zhao Bo and Huang Yang) Exports suffered another five consecutive months of declines, with the manufacturing purchasing managers’ index (PMI) contracting for seven straight months, and the consumer price index (CPI) again hitting “three-digit territory”… In recent times, the authorities in Taiwan have successively released January economic data for 2023.
Experts analyze that Taiwan's economy struggled to show good performance at the beginning of the year, with considerable growth pressure.
According to the Financial Affairs Bureau of the Taiwan authorities, Taiwan’s exports in January this year were $31.51 billion, down 21.2% year-on-year and falling for the fifth consecutive month.
The export value of the 11 major export categories has declined compared to the same period last year.
Rubber and plastics, as well as their products, and optical equipment saw the steepest declines, with year-over-year reductions of 37.6% and 35.7%, respectively.
Exports of electronic parts decreased by 20.1% per year, the largest decrease in 11 years.
Among them, integrated circuits declined 18.3% year-on-year, marking the largest drop in 14 years.
The department's head of statistics, Domina, said that this shows that the weakness of consumer electronics demand is spreading, and the electronics industry is entering a period of correction.
Statistics show that Taiwan's imports and exports both declined in January, with a trade surplus of only $2.34 billion, the lowest level in nearly three years.
The Taiwanese government's financial affairs authority believes that the global demand for terminals is declining, industry adjustments to inventory suppress the willingness of suppliers to buy, the export momentum is unlikely to improve in the short term, and Taiwan is facing a recession in exports in the first quarter of this year that is higher than expected.
According to the Central Institute of Economic Management in Taiwan, the seasonally adjusted Purchasing Managers' Index (PMI) for Taiwan's manufacturing sector in January this year was 40.4%, down 3.3 percentage points from December last year and contracting for seven consecutive months.
In the economic monitoring index system, PMI is at 50% as the turning point for health and illness; an index greater than 50% indicates expansion of prosperity, while less than 50% signifies contraction.
In January, five components of Taiwan's PMI contracted in new orders, production, employment, and delivery times to suppliers, while inventories tightened.
All six major industries are reporting PMI contraction, with contraction speeds in descending order as follows: electrical and mechanical equipment industry (35.1%), electronic and optical industry (35.2%), chemical and biopharmaceutical healthcare industry (39.2%), basic materials industry (42.4%), transportation equipment industry (42.6%), and food and textile industry (45.7%).
In terms of prices, the Taiwanese government's Office of the Chief Accountant announced that Taiwan's annual CPI growth rate was 3.04 percent in January this year, breaking another 3 percent since July last year.
Among them, vegetable prices have skyrocketed by 28.25%, reaching a new 17-month high.
Committee Chairperson Mr. Cao Zhihong from the “Director General’s Office of Statistics,” acknowledged that price increases had exceeded expectations. Even if we exclude factors such as the Spring Festival and other seasonal influences, the year-on-year inflation rate for January and February this year should be close to the 2.71% in December last year. Inflationary pressure is still present, albeit at high levels.
Looking ahead to Taiwan’s economy this year, experts are pessimistic according to reporting from media outlets such as “United Daily News” and Yahoo Finance on the island.
Professor Wu Daren from the “Central University of Taiwan’s School of Economics” has warned that exports slowing down could result in cash flow problems for export manufacturing firms and higher risks of defaulting on debt.
At the same time, falling orders have caused producers to reduce labor costs and impact the labor market and household economies, which in turn hit consumption capacity.
According to Qiu Dasheng, a researcher at the Taiwan Economic Research Institute, the inflation situation in Europe and the United States has not been resolved this year, demand has continued to shrink and the decline in Taiwan ' s exports is expected to continue into the first half of the year.
As Taiwan's economy relies on exports and is affected by the export slump, economic growth throughout the year will not be as strong as last year.
New members of the Central Committee, alternate members, and leading officials at provincial and ministerial levels complete training on studying Xi Jinping's Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China - Latest News - Hunan Daily Network - Huanasohua News Online
The newly elected members of the Politburo Standing Committee and alternate members of the Central Committee as well as leading cadres at provincial and ministerial levels have completed their training on learning and implementing Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China.
2023-02-11 13:07:20 [Source: Xinhua News Agency] [Editor-in-Chief: Li Shuxue] Font size: [Large Medium Small]
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 10 – The seminar for new members of the Central Committee, alternate members, and senior officials from provinces and ministries to study and implement Xi Jinping’s New Era of Socialism with Chinese Characteristics and the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China concluded late today at the Central Party School (National Administration Institute). Chairman of the Political Bureau and Secretary of the Secretariat of the CPC Central Committee, Ma Xiaotian, attended the closing ceremony and delivered a closing speech.
He stated that to thoroughly study and implement President Xi Jinping’s important speech at the opening ceremony of the seminar, one must further strengthen support for “two establishments” and resolutely uphold “two maintenances,” enhance their abilities, and work diligently in practice. They should strive to advance all aspects of China’s modernization in an all-round way, achieving accomplishments that can withstand the test of history, practice, and the people in the process of comprehensively building a modern socialist society and comprehensively advancing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.
During the seminar, all participants guided by Xi Jinping's Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era, studied in depth the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China and President Xi Jinping's opening remarks at the seminar's start. They engaged in in-depth discussions and exchanges based on actual circumstances, deepening their understanding of a series of major theoretical and practical issues concerning China's modernization. This strengthened their confidence and determination to advance the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation under the strong leadership of the Central Committee with Comrade Xi Jinping at its core. It also heightened their sense of responsibility and mission to perform their duties, do their work well, and ensure a good start to the new era and new journey.
At the graduation ceremony, 10 representatives from the seminar spoke, reporting on their learning gains and exchanging experiences.
Zai Cai Qi’s statement, studying and implementing Xi Jinping’s Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China is both a primary political task in the current and future period, and a long-term strategic task. It should be carried out according to the requirement of “comprehensively learning, comprehensively grasping, and fully implementing.” This will push the work of studying and implementing these ideas to go deeper, more practically, and more deeply into people’s hearts.
To more deeply grasp the decisive significance of “two establishment,” to uphold the core position of Xi Jinping and the authority and centralized unified leadership of the Party Central Committee resolutely, and to continuously improve one’s political judgment, political insight, and political execution capabilities, always maintaining high consistency in terms of ideology, politics, and actions with the Party Central Committee with Comrade Xi Jinping at its core.
We must strive to master this vision of Marxist theory, consciously use the Party's innovative theories to arm our minds, guide our practices, advance our work, work hard in deep learning, insight, and diligence, to truly learn firm beliefs, to learn absolute loyalty, and to learn mission responsibilities.
To earnestly implement all decisions and deployments of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China with an enterprising spirit, advance the Chinese-style modernization, roll up our sleeves to work hard, get down to business as a good “construction supervisor”, step by step turn the blueprint into reality.
To remember that reforming and governing the Party in an all-round way is an ongoing process and that self-revolution of the Party must also be ongoing, and to press hard for the political responsibility of comprehensive strict governance of the Party, with political building of the Party as its overarching priority, and advance the new great project of Party building in this new era.
To enhance our ability to promote high-quality development, serve the people, and manage and prevent risks, we must foster a strong tradition of investigation and research. We must resolutely prevent and overcome formalism and bureaucratism.
Zhai Qingfeng, Li Jianjie, Li Shulei, Chen Wenqing, Liu Jinguo, and Wang Xiaohong attended the graduation ceremony, with Chen Xi presiding over the ceremony.
VIENTIANE – VNA Special Correspondent reports that Vietnam’s Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh and his spouse successfully concluded official visits to Singapore and Brunei, achieving comprehensive, pragmatic, and specific results.
During his three-day visit to Singapore and Brunei, Premier Pham Minh Chinh attended over 30 different activities.
The achievements have injected new momentum into further deepening, broadening, and enhancing both the strategic partnership between Vietnam and Laos and the comprehensive partnership between Vietnam and the EU.
During his visit to both countries, Prime Minister Fan Mingjing continued to reaffirm the Viet Nam Party and the country ' s external routes, namely independence, pluralism and change, and was ready to be good friends and reliable partners for all countries, as well as responsible members of the international community.
Strengthening relations with Singapore and Brunei is each country’s need, aimed at enhancing the well-being of its people, and committed to peace, stability, and development in the region and the world.
During each meeting and negotiation, Mr. Fan Mingzheng agreed with their respective leaders from Singapore and Brunei to strengthen political trust in Vietnam through inter-governmental visits of high-level delegations as well as effective implementation of bilateral cooperation mechanisms and key partnership agreements.
Several cooperation documents were signed during this visit.
Among these, two major highlights include the Memorandum of Understanding on Green and Digital Economy Partnership signed with Singapore and the Action Plan for Strengthening Comprehensive Partnership between Vietnam and Brunei Darussalam for the 2023-2027 Period.
Vietnam and Singapore have signed a Memorandum of Understanding on Green and Digital Economy Partnership.
Image from Vietnam News Agency
During meetings with business leaders, seminars, and economic forums, Premier Pham Minh Chinh emphasized that Vietnam welcomes and creates favorable conditions for Singapore and Brunei enterprises to expand their investment scope in areas such as digital transformation, green energy, high-tech, and innovation and creativity in Vietnam.
This visit not only helps to deepen cooperation between Vietnam and Singapore and Brunei in traditional areas such as politics, diplomacy, economy, security, defense, education and training, oil and gas, tourism, people-to-people exchanges, but also creates frameworks for cooperation in new potential areas such as digital economy, green economy, energy transition, innovation and creativity, smart cities, and sustainable development.
King Hassanal Bolkiah of Brunei and Prime Minister Fan Ming are preparing for a bilateral symposium.
Image sourced from VNA News Agency
During his visits to both countries, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh made time to visit and listen to the concerns and aspirations of the Vietnamese community residing there.
During their leaders' meeting, Premier Pham Minh Chinh suggested that both countries’ authorities pay more attention to ensuring fair treatment for the local Vietnamese community, provide them with opportunities to contribute to local society, and create favorable conditions to foster relations between the two countries.
The proposals have been endorsed and supported by both leaders.
In particular, the Prime Minister also shared with the leaders of the two countries the desire for an ASEAN Community of unity, peace, stability and prosperity; unanimously agreed to maintain cooperation in solidarity with ASEAN countries and enhance ASEAN's central role in the complex and changing context of regional and international situations.
With the significant achievements achieved, Prime Minister Van Minh's official visit to Singapore and Brunei has been instrumental in the effective implementation of the 13th Foreign Route as a priority for strengthening relations with ASEAN neighbours, in the effective implementation of the 12th Conclusion of the Political Bureau of the Communist Party of Vietnam (CPC) on the new situation in Vietnam, and in contributing positively to the strengthening of national unity.
(The End)
What exactly was "the object" that was shot down over Alaska?
Confused, speculation abounds.
The US military shot down a unidentified object flying over Alaska near its coast on Friday afternoon (February 10th) using the US' most advanced stealth fighter jet, the F-22.
The spot where it was shot down is ten miles off the Alaskan coast.
This is the second time American military has downed an airborne object in less than a week.
An air balloon operated from China that was spying on American communications in US airspace drifted for several days before it was shot down off the South Carolina coastline of the United States last Saturday.
The Pentagon said the second object to be shot down entered U.S. airspace for the first time on Thursday night and was tracked by the U.S. military as it moved over northeastern Alaska, flying at an altitude of 12,000 meters (40,000 feet), about the size of a small car and much smaller than the Chinese spy balloon that was shot down earlier.
The Pentagon also believes that there is currently no indication that the object is manoeuvrable.
The White House National Security Council strategic communication coordinator, John Kirby, stated on Friday that, while the specifics of the object flying at high altitude were not yet clear, it posed “a reasonable threat to the safety of civil aviation aircraft”.
Kobe stated that the object is different from the spy balloon discovered in the United States, which did not have a payload hanging from it.
Kobe said, “We refer to it as an ‘object’ is the best description we can make at this moment.”
President Biden listened to the Pentagon's suggestions before ordering the shooting down of the object, and he made the decision very carefully, Kobe added.
The US official description of the object can be roughly summarized as follows: it is about the size of a small car; there is no steering wheel or suspension system; its flight height is around 10,000 meters.
But these pieces of information still fail to address fundamental questions such as what this object is, which country it belongs to, and what task it is performing.
There are many analyses and speculations on the Internet that this could be another Chinese balloon.
It may come from China, like the spy balloon that invaded American airspace and the Chinese balloon that floated over Latin America, and they perform certain missions in different locations.
Some have linked this "object" from Alaska to unidentified flying objects (UFOs).
The report by US Newsweek quotes a tweet from US former Representative Peter Meijer on Friday saying, "I wish this unidentified flying object was also a spy balloon instead of a legitimate UFO."
The irony of equating extraterrestrial spacecraft with weather balloons is amusing, but that does not warrant an interstellar conflict, Marks said.
Major sent this tweet shortly after Kirby confirmed that the object in Alaska had been shot down.
According to Newsweek, the object was suspected of being a UFO and not just a Major.
Republican Representative Tim Burchett of Tennessee criticized the government's cover-up of intelligence last month and demanded that the Office of the Director of National Intelligence release reports on "unidentified flying objects."
Iran marks Revolution anniversary as hackers attack President's televised speech in support of protesters
The Islamic Republic of Iran held an official rally on Saturday to commemorate the 44th anniversary of the Iranian Revolution, but anti-government hackers briefly interrupted President Ibrahim Lacy's televised address.
The television address made by President’s live-streaming speech was interrupted for about a minute and then appeared a group of anti-Iranian government hackers with the name Edalat Ali (Ali Justice).
There was also a voice screaming for the death of the Islamic Republic.
According to a report today by Reuters, hackers disrupted coverage of a national TV station in Iran as the country commemorated the anniversary of the revolution.
As Iran officially commemorates the 44th anniversary of the Iranian Revolution, Lacey's hardline government faces the toughest challenge of the young protesters demanding their resignation, but Lacey still calls on the deceived youths to repent so they can be pardoned by Iran's supreme leader.
Protests swept across Iran following the death of 22-year-old Mahsa Amini, who died in custody by the country's morality police in September.
The Iranian security forces have ruthlessly suppressed protests, making this one of the most powerful challenges to Islamic Republic since the overthrow of the monarchy in 1979.
As part of an amnesty commemorating the Revolutionary Anniversary, Iranian authorities on Friday released imprisoned dissidents Farhad Mesami and Iranian-French scholar Fariba Adelha from hunger strike protests.
Earlier Ayatollah Ali Khameini issued an amnesty decree that included some prisoners arrested during recent anti-government protests.
According to the human rights group HRANA, as of Friday, 528 protesters have been killed, including 71 minors.
The report says that another 70 government security personnel were killed.
It is believed that up to 19,763 protesters were arrested.
For weeks, Iranian leaders and official media have been calling for a vote at Saturday's rallies to express opposition to the protests and support for the government.
On Friday night, on the eve of the anniversary of the Iranian Revolution, the official media showed fireworks as part of a government-sponsored celebration, and people chanted "Allahu Akbar!"
(God is the greatest!)
However, one can also hear many people shouting "Death to the dictator!" at the rally.
And death of the Islamic Republic in videos posted on social media.
On Saturday, government television broadcast live videos of official state gatherings across the country.
In Tehran, as part of the official celebration, national anti-ballistic missiles, drones, anti-submarine cruisers and other military equipment were displayed.
President Lacey's speech was frequently interrupted by the slogan “Die America” — a signpost at a state rally.
The crowd also shouted “Death to Israel”.
According to Reuters, Adelkhah, who has been in prison since 2019, is one of seven French nationals detained in Iran, a factor in the deterioration of relations between Paris and Tehran in recent months.
She was sentenced to five years in prison in 2020 on charges of national security violations.
They later placed her under house arrest, but in January she returned to prison.
Adelkhah denied the allegations.
And just a week before Mesa was released, supporters warned that he was at risk of death due to his hunger strike.
He was arrested in 2018 for protesting against the forced wearing of a headscarf.
The French Ministry of Foreign Affairs, in response to the release of Adelkhah on Friday, called for the restoration of her freedom “including that she should be allowed to return to France if she so wishes.
